<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Loja, Spain</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Loja is a town in the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, on the Genil River west of the city of Granada. A fortress of the Nasrid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> of Granada guarding the western approach to its capital, it resisted a Castilian siege in 1482 but was taken by Ferdinand and Isabella in 1486, a key step in the conquest of Granada.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/loja-spain.jpg" alt="Loja, Spain" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Loja_Campanario.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
